# Paper

- **Precondition: the senior author decides the title, the framing and which experiments go into the paper.** Until
  then `paper/main.tex` stays a format skeleton with empty tables — do not write the abstract, introduction,
  contributions or any prose, and do not pick experiments on the senior's behalf. The rules below apply once the
  framing is fixed.
- Official ICASSP 2027 kit is in `paper/` (`spconf.sty`, `IEEEbib.bst`; samples in `paper/official_kit/`). The manuscript
  base is `old_reference.tex` at the repo root (the team's ICASSP 2026 paper, re-aligned to the 2027 kit; D-033) +
  `paper/refs.bib`; `paper/main.tex` is the earlier skeleton kept for reference. The three cohort tables in
  `old_reference.tex` are generated by `scripts/build_dataset_tables.py --splice old_reference.tex`; never edit them by hand. 4 pages of technical content + optional 5th page with references /
  funding / ethics statement only; PDF ≤ 5 MB; filename = first author's surname; single-blind; every author
  needs an ORCID; disclose AI-assisted content in the acknowledgments (IEEE policy).
- Every number in the paper must trace to one row of `outputs/analysis/snn_round/<dataset>/*.csv` or
  `results_snapshot_2026-09-13/**/tables/*.csv`. Build tables from those CSVs; do not compute by hand.
- Candidate framing from plan v2 (NOT adopted until the senior says so): non-inferiority (δ = 1pp = spread of the
  top-8 ANNs on 2C) + alignment × network-type interaction + energy with EEGNet/S-EEGNet as reference. Whatever the
  framing, cite and contrast Zhang et al. 2025 (Neural Networks, PLIF+EA),
  NiSNN-A (TNNLS 2025), HR-SNN, LENet/SRIF, Yin–Corradi–Bohté 2021, Perez-Nieves 2021, PLIF (ICCV 2021),
  He & Wu 2020 (EA), Junqueira 2024, Wimpff 2024, Horowitz 2014 + Dampfhoffer 2023.
- Forbidden phrasings: "posterior drift"; "anytime / streaming" (say sample-synchronous, look-ahead ≤ 128 ms with
  'same' padding); "LIF = envelope detector" (say LIF₁ rectifies at threshold → conv2 smooths → envelope estimate);
  "1-bit encoding preserves phase so spatial filtering is valid" as a theorem (it is a hypothesis supported by the
  `afe` ablation); any energy multiplier in the title.
- Limitations to state: transductive alignment, single training seed / shared init, recipe dependence, SHU floor
  effect, temporal-native model ~3× slower (launch-bound).
- Login node has pdfLaTeX since 2026-09-19 (`~/.TinyTeX`, `~/.local/bin/{pdflatex,bibtex,latexmk}`; tectonic is a
  XeTeX fallback that needs an OT1 wrapper for Times). Compile copies under `/tmp`; the final PDF still comes from
  Overleaf / pdfLaTeX (see `paper/README.md`).
